# editor / agent scratch
# "When NYC Government Goes Open Source by Default" — a draft roadmap that is
# NOT for this public repo. It now lives in its own PRIVATE repo:
#   https://github.com/sarapis/open-source-by-default  (~/Antigravity/open-source-by-default)
# The local copy here was deleted once that repo existed, so there is one source
# rather than two that can drift. This entry stays as a guard against re-adding.
#
# ⚠ Untracking never unpublished it. The draft was pushed publicly in four
# commits (8462c02, 6f3e02e, 5f7b029, ab1b6f7) and those versions remain readable
# in this repo's history on GitHub — a deliberate decision, since the content is
# sourced public facts, not anything sensitive.
docs/OPEN-SOURCE-BY-DEFAULT.md

# `.claude/*`, NOT `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negation below is silently ignored with the
# trailing-slash form. Ignoring the contents instead makes it work.
.claude/*
# Shared project settings are tracked: they carry the PreToolUse hook that
# refuses blanket `git add -A` here, and it has to reach the other sessions and
# clones it exists to protect. launch.json and settings.local.json stay local.
!.claude/settings.json
